MTCC: Mazorcaz's Tiny C Compiler
--------------------------------

MTCC is a small self hosting C compiler I made
mostly for fun and to learn more about C.

It primarily targets a subset of C11, with
no VLA or obscure feature support.

PROJECT STRUCTURE & BUILDING
----------------------------

All .c and .h files are in ./src/. To build,
you simply just cc ./src/*.c -o bin/mtcc.
The script ./make.sh does this.

Incremental building is not necessary for
small projects like this.

STYLE GUIDE
-----------

Unless specified, stick to the Linux Kernel
style guide (https://docs.kernel.org/process/coding-style.html).

 - At the top of the file is a comment with the file name
   (e.g. /* main.c */)

 - Header guards are prefixed with MTCC_ (e.g. MTCC_MAIN_H).

 - When init functions fail, free functions need not be called.
   But when a non-init function fails, the free function must
   be called on the object before exiting.
